    "narrative": "With today\u2019s limited slate, the Austin Waves offense centers heavily on our C1 and UTIL spots. **Drake Baldwin** stands as our strongest play with a score of 55.29, bolstered by a prime #4 spot in the order which provides the RBI opportunities necessary to remain competitive in a tight Roto race. While facing Aaron Nola presents a challenge, **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s recent form and park factors keep him in the \"Marginal-to-Strong\" tier. Conversely, **Dominic Smith** checks in at a 46.12. While his raw base projection is lower, the +7% platoon advantage against the right-handed Nola prevents him from falling into the \"Below floor\" category, despite the efficiency drag from his likely #8 spot in the lineup.\n\nThe primary frustration today remains the inactivity of our core offensive anchors. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all sidelined by team off-days, our scoring ceiling is significantly suppressed, putting extra pressure on the fringe roster to produce. Furthermore, we continue to monitor **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, as his absence deprives us of the elite sprint speed necessary to chip away at the SB category. Given the thin options, **Dominic Smith** was the closest call for the bench; however, with no other viable hitters available to rotate in, he remains locked in to ensure we maximize our daily game caps.\n\nRisks remain elevated as both active players are operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status, meaning these scores are based on historical order assumptions that could shift. If **Drake Baldwin** or **Dominic Smith** are shuffled down the lineup once official cards are exchanged, their efficiency scores will drop immediately, potentially forcing a move toward the bench to preserve games for more favorable matchups later in the week. We are also tracking limited availability for the rest of our prospects, including **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara**, all of whom are restricted by the current schedule volatility.",
